#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186475912 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119837 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "caf29808-4551-56a0-ac86-a4587a06fc0f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intersection Point of a Line and a Plane Given in Other Forms"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "007d69dc-a2ca-580f-b0f7-74cbcfa1ebdd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475444} {:answer/id #uuid "3a25e529-3954-5987-92eb-d533381cc44b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(25,31,-6)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475523} {:answer/id #uuid "52af092c-e727-5f18-8ff7-345347fe6d51" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-8,-13,5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475562} {:answer/id #uuid "572842f6-cb5d-5a22-b2c9-50266f22eb6a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(13,15,-2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475570} {:answer/id #uuid "fca47535-789f-5b0b-98b2-271a04ca1b25" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-14,-21,7)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475823}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3a25e529-3954-5987-92eb-d533381cc44b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(25,31,-6)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475523} :answer-field/id #uuid "d8937436-576e-5320-a137-6b981c96167e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475895}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "07e33caa-9650-5834-8d9a-46cc82f723d1" :question/math-academy-id "q-108434" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:r=⟨1,-1,2⟩+w⟨3,4,-1⟩,\\,Π:r=⟨5,3,-4⟩+s⟨1,0,2⟩+t⟨0,-2,3⟩.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "From the equation of a plane in the parametric form $r=p+tv+sw$, we have that its normal vector is $n=v\\times w.$ In our case, the normal vectors to $Π$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =v\\times w \\\\  & =⟨1,0,2⟩\\times ⟨0,-2,3⟩ \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =4i-3j-2k \\\\  & =⟨4,-3,-2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the plane $Π$ in dot product form is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨4,-3,-2⟩ & =⟨5,3,-4⟩\\cdot ⟨4,-3,-2⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨4,-3,-2⟩ & =19.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨1,-1,2⟩+w⟨3,4,-1⟩$ into the equation of the plane in dot product form, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨4,-3,-2⟩ & =19 \\\\ ⟨1+3w,-1+4w,2-w⟩\\cdot ⟨4,-3,-2⟩ & =19 \\\\ 4(1+3w)-3(-1+4w)-2(2-w) & =19 \\\\ 4+12w+3-12w-4+2w & =19 \\\\ 2w & =16 \\\\ w & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to get the position vector $q$ of the intersection point $Q,$ we substitute $w=8$ into the equation of the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}q & =⟨1+3(8),-1+4(8),2-8⟩ \\\\  & =⟨25,31,-6⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection point is $Q(25,31,-6).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120290 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119838 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "82e761b5-ec1c-549d-b726-e0909cfe460b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intersection Point of a Line in Parametric Form and a Plane in Cartesian Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a523b91-b0c8-5d77-ac05-a918d500094c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-9,9,7)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312052} {:answer/id #uuid "82d8d2f3-12d7-5f69-9c67-b4d2db7dc5da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313028} {:answer/id #uuid "8d14825a-42af-51a3-9f03-b6163ac5f748" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(5,-1,3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313102} {:answer/id #uuid "95ed7638-8aa8-5f1b-b639-82099d0d033c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(9,7,-9)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313173} {:answer/id #uuid "c5ba162d-d3e7-561c-ba10-731b0f92f98b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(9,-9,7)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313525}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c5ba162d-d3e7-561c-ba10-731b0f92f98b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(9,-9,7)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313525} :answer-field/id #uuid "0d7ba987-d1b7-522f-859e-b04e23ff46bc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314051}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c755ffbb-8374-5c52-a967-a6387ef6da9c" :question/math-academy-id "q-33992" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:\\{\\begin{aligned}x=5-2t \\\\ y=-1+4t \\\\ z=-3-5t\\end{aligned}\\,\\text{and}\\,Π:2x-5y+3z-84=0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We can substitute the parametric expressions for $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ of the line into the equation of the plane immediately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x-5y+3z-84 & =0 \\\\ 2(5-2t)-5(-1+4t)+3(-3-5t) & =84 \\\\ 10-4t+5-20t-9-15t & =84 \\\\ -39t & =78 \\\\ t & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$, we substitute $t=-2$ into the parametric equations of the line:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x=5-2(-2)=9 \\\\ y=-1+4(-2)=-9 \\\\ z=-3-5(-2)=7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection point is  $P(9,-9,7).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186484201 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119838 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "82e761b5-ec1c-549d-b726-e0909cfe460b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intersection Point of a Line in Parametric Form and a Plane in Cartesian Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "20fc86f8-0368-54eb-a3e0-3cf6b0379332" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-16,-16,13)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483621} {:answer/id #uuid "2143e54b-67d5-5002-957a-3bf88c230ca4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(24,-11,11)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483624} {:answer/id #uuid "257b548a-b52d-5b2d-8a2f-57d74b50d39c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483630} {:answer/id #uuid "7944f3e7-3b31-5e5a-b5cb-a1562208eb42" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(11,-13,11)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483813} {:answer/id #uuid "a0a4f2b9-c6e0-5e67-8ab6-66d592472d45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(26,12,12)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483899}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "20fc86f8-0368-54eb-a3e0-3cf6b0379332" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-16,-16,13)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483621} :answer-field/id #uuid "15f90597-4c03-5ae4-b2c2-f42eae091087" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186484091}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "12b4f5c6-720f-5c2c-b1e8-295eb7dcb29c" :question/math-academy-id "q-73991" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:\\{\\begin{aligned}x=-2-2t \\\\ y=5-3t \\\\ z=-1+2t\\end{aligned}\\,\\text{and}\\,Π:3x-2y+6z=62.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We can substitute the parametric expressions for $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ of the line into the equation of the plane immediately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x-2y+6z & =62 \\\\ 3(-2-2t)-2(5-3t)+6(-1+2t) & =62 \\\\ -6-6t-10+6t-6+12t & =62 \\\\ 12t & =84 \\\\ t & =7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$, we substitute $t=6$ into the parametric equations of the line:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x=-2-2(7)=-16 \\\\ y=5-3(7)=-16 \\\\ z=-1+2(7)=13\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection point is $P(-16,-16,13).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342127 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119838 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "82e761b5-ec1c-549d-b726-e0909cfe460b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intersection Point of a Line in Parametric Form and a Plane in Cartesian Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1b2ccf68-fbc4-58ea-80f0-c47a1f4e61c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339365} {:answer/id #uuid "1d364631-26c0-59a4-93c9-0842ba8027a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(19,10,16)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339381} {:answer/id #uuid "2bfe2f6a-4b05-5041-9be9-ec95d41ced84" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(18,8,12)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339510} {:answer/id #uuid "90fc5ea2-94e0-5824-91af-e274368bde07" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(18,11,16)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340429} {:answer/id #uuid "a5f82de1-4dec-5d15-9285-344580d1aa1f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(8,-1,6)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340633}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "90fc5ea2-94e0-5824-91af-e274368bde07" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(18,11,16)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340429} :answer-field/id #uuid "3769c405-5ffb-59ea-8180-d6fbf6837b56" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341479}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8a17e320-306c-50fa-b84b-f8cbe958e629" :question/math-academy-id "q-73993" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:\\{\\begin{aligned}x=3-5t \\\\ y=2-3t \\\\ z=-2-6t\\end{aligned}\\,\\text{and}\\,Π:5x-2y+4z-132=0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We can substitute the parametric expressions for $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ of the line into the equation of the plane immediately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5x-2y+4z-132 & =0 \\\\ 5(3-5t)-2(2-3t)+4(-2-6t) & =132 \\\\ 15-25t-4+6t-8-24t & =132 \\\\ -43t & =129 \\\\ t & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$, we substitute $t=-3$ into the parametric equations of the line:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x=3-5(-3)=18 \\\\ y=2-3(-3)=11 \\\\ z=-2-6(-3)=16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection point is  $P(18,11,16).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342129 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119837 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "caf29808-4551-56a0-ac86-a4587a06fc0f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intersection Point of a Line and a Plane Given in Other Forms"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8e017315-e476-5fa0-8361-dc00652a6489" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2,0,1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340405} {:answer/id #uuid "ad64653c-387b-56c4-988a-77711f82ccae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340706} {:answer/id #uuid "af463bcf-e431-5d1e-a420-7660e1b98031" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-2,-5,4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340726} {:answer/id #uuid "d8153fa3-e604-533d-b56e-b26114f3d4d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3,1,5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341045} {:answer/id #uuid "f86bd550-c5e7-5c4a-ad94-8436818324a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-5,4,2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341326}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d8153fa3-e604-533d-b56e-b26114f3d4d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3,1,5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341045} :answer-field/id #uuid "9343b686-98f1-53b8-a0c6-e7d798a3b52a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341638}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "156769fc-4325-56fe-a6f3-a488d1baa118" :question/math-academy-id "q-74004" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:r=⟨3,1,5⟩+w⟨-2,-5,4⟩,\\,Π:r=⟨-5,4,2⟩+s⟨0,3,1⟩+t⟨2,0,1⟩.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "From the equation of a plane in the parametric form $r=p+tv+sw$, we have that its normal vector is $n=v\\times w.$ In our case, the normal vectors to $Π$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =v\\times w \\\\  & =⟨0,3,1⟩\\times ⟨2,0,1⟩ \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 0 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =3i+2j-6k \\\\  & =⟨3,2,-6⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the plane $Π$ in dot product form is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨3,2,-6⟩ & =⟨-5,4,2⟩\\cdot ⟨3,2,-6⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨3,2,-6⟩ & =-19.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨3,1,5⟩+w⟨-2,-5,4⟩$ into the equation of the plane in dot product form, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨3,2,-6⟩ & =-19 \\\\ ⟨3-2w,1-5w,5+4w⟩\\cdot ⟨3,2,-6⟩ & =-19 \\\\ 3(3-2w)+2(1-5w)-6(5+4w) & =-19 \\\\ 9-6w+2-10w-30-24w & =-19 \\\\ -40w & =0 \\\\ w & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to get the position vector $q$ of the intersection point $Q,$ we substitute $w=0$ into the equation of the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}q & =⟨3-2(0),1-5(0),5+4(0)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,1,5⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection point is $Q(3,1,5).$"}]}
